/* GAME:above:BEGIN */
/* ---- Phase 32D: The View from Above, developed — Marcus Aurelius's "An Emperor's Laurel" ----
   Idea check: playing this, you feel a worry shrink to a speck as you rise, and then you come back down to do small, real duties with a lighter
   heart. That is Marcus Aurelius's view from above, and his reminder to get up and do the work of a human being.
   Stages: I · Rising (the tent at night, a huge worry cloud over it. At each of five levels one small detail glows: the lamp, a sentry fire, the river,
   the roads, a star. Tap it, or press A, to take it in; until then rising does nothing. Hold B, hold up, or pinch in to rise; letting go holds the view)
   → II · The Quiet (the earth under the stars. Hold B for four breaths, about sixteen seconds; letting go pauses the count and never resets it. The stars
   turn slowly and the cloud fades to a faint speck) → III · The Return (hold A, hold down, or spread two fingers to come back down fast; the little cloud
   comes along, small and quiet. At the tent, tap a duty and Marcus walks over and does it: answer a letter, feed the horse, thank the guard. All three is the win).
   The zoom: one value s.z, 0 (the tent fills the stage) to 4 (the earth). MINI_ART.above.zoom[k]={cx,cy,s} says where scene k sits inside scene k+1.
   view(z) is the one function that places the scenes. For z in [k,k+1], u=z-k: scene k+1 is drawn with scale S=s_k^(u-1) as a true zoom about the fixed
   point F=((cx,cy)-s(96,160))/(1-s), so at u=0 scene k's inset (scene k+1 at 1/s) fills the stage and at u=1 scene k+1 does; scene k is drawn on top as the inset
   (scene k+1's transform composed with the registration) and fades out over the step. Every scene's transform is also exposed (xfs), and the worry cloud, which lives
   in scene 0 and never changes its world size, takes its place and size from scene 0's transform. With Reduce Motion nothing is scaled: scene k crossfades into k+1.
   State: s.z (zoom), s.lvl (the last whole level reached), s.taken[5], s.bt (seconds of breath held, 0..16), s.wasted (a tap that missed a glowing detail that was not yet taken in),
   s.dutyMiss (a tap on no undone duty), s.duties [{k,x,y,hx,hy,done}], s.mq (queued duties), s.mw (the job Marcus is on: walk | act), s.mx/s.my (Marcus),
   s.cp (the little cloud in Stage III), s.tq (taps waiting 0.15 s so a pinch can cancel them), s.pdir (the pinch latch: -1 in, +1 out). */
